Lab 19: Troubleshooting ODF Using Ansible
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Implement Ansible automation for troubleshooting OpenShift Data Foundation (ODF) storage issues
Utilize Ansible facts and Kubernetes/OpenShift collections to verify ODF system state
Develop a playbook that detects common ODF problems (failed PVCs, unhealthy Ceph pods)
Generate structured troubleshooting reports from playbook run data
Configure a validation playbook that checks ODF state against defined rules
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of OpenShift Container Platform concepts
Familiarity with OpenShift Data Foundation (ODF) components (CephCluster, OSD pods, storage classes)
Knowledge of Ansible fundamentals including playbooks, tasks, and modules
Experience with YAML and Jinja2 template syntax
Understanding of Kubernetes/OpenShift CLI commands
Basic Linux command line skills
Required tools must be installed on the Ansible control node:

python3 -m pip install --user ansible kubernetes
ansible-galaxy collection install kubernetes.core
ansible-galaxy collection install community.general
